<statement>
<p>
	This function uses &lt;pf&gt;ginput&lt;/pf&gt; to get the coordinates of a point from the user, and continues to &quot;request&quot; a point until the user clicks on a valid point.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>no</pf> number — function inputs</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>x</pf> (double) double — is the x-coordinate of the point</p>
			<p><pf>y</pf> (double) double — is the y-coordinate of the point</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>In order to test this function, it may be helpful to have a primitive mock-up of the game board to view. You may use</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>this script</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>while you are testing. DO NOT CALL THE SCRIPT/USE THIS CODE IN ANY OF THE PROGRAMS/SCRIPTS YOU SUBMIT.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
